      "message": "Let a claim cover existing code, and draw the debt coming down\n\nCode that arrived by import was never judged here, and until now the\nonly way its debt fell was a rewrite. A claim may now say what existing\ncode its command exercises. When the change carrying it lands and a\nthird-party runner has reproduced it, every line under those paths is\nbacked by that claim, whatever landed the line; a cover nobody re-ran is\nshown and moves nothing, and a cover never lowers a line. The forge\nredraws the map after every landing and keeps its counts at each tip, so\nthe Verification tab draws the burndown and credits each author with the\nlines their reproduced covers moved. An owner turns the most indebted\nfiles into tasks with one button, each saying which lines are short of\nwhat and how the claim must be written, and the task lands with the\nchange that pays it down.\n\nChange-Id: Iburndown0080covers\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
